ainst is  forces  back then he didn't know if his family  was alive or dead  the couple rarely talk about what they  experienced they're too preoccupied with  trying to discover the fate of their  three missing children  we ask around everywhere we even ask aid  workers  and people smugglers who free abducted  people whether they can help us  believe me whenever someone's freed i go  there the same day  or the next morning at the latest and i  ask  but so far his efforts have been in vain  over 2 000 yazidi families live on mount  sinjar  and almost all have family members  missing  a few months ago a child care facility  was set up at this camp  it's open for two hours a day  today eight-year-old hannah reads out  what's written on the board  [Music]  but most of all the social workers want  the children to have fun  [Applause]  we don't discuss  sometimes kocha has no idea how to ease  her children's pain  they all suffer from nightmares the is  men kept taking the children  to make kocha obey them  they were held in a cellar without any  light for months on end  in desperation she tattooed their names  on their arms  using a nail and ash for ink  i did it so that they wouldn't forget  their names  when they took the children away from me  is would give them new names  but then the leader said if i see a name  on an arm  i'll cut off that arm so i stopped look  here  i only did half her name  has taken precautions to ensure that his  family will never go through anything  like this again  he's got a kalashnikov hidden in the  closet  next time he says he won't be afraid to  use it  i've learned from the past we trusted  our neighbors then  they said they were our friends but they  killed us yazidis  i need a weapon to defend my family  we're afraid  while the family is eating lunch mahmud  is called outside  german aid agency vailtongahefe is  looking for workers at the refugee camp  the men can earn 300 u.s dollars in six  days  but some of the men here aren't on